{"jobs":[{"id":"29227b2e-3faf-49c6-b347-9791bd9b4b73","title":"Senior DevOps Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Dallas, TX","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York City","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T16:58:47.253+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/29227b2e-3faf-49c6-b347-9791bd9b4b73","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/29227b2e-3faf-49c6-b347-9791bd9b4b73/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Senior DevOps Engineer</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>'s infrastructure is the layer on which everything else depends. Our marketplace, integrations, data warehouse, and clinical workflows all run on a cloud environment that must be reliable, observable, secure, and compliant with the frameworks governing healthcare technology. As we scale, that layer needs to scale with us, and the engineering practices around it need to mature at the same pace.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a <strong>Senior DevOps Engineer</strong> to join our Infrastructure team as we expand the DevOps function. This is a hands-on senior role that combines deep technical execution with the kind of engineering judgment that shapes how a growing infrastructure team operates. You will report into our Infrastructure leadership and work closely with Engineering, Security, and Compliance across a HIPAA-regulated environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide hands-on DevOps work across the network, servers, and cloud platforms, operating as a senior technical contributor from day one</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure DevOps and Engineering processes align with security best practices, and help embed those practices deeper into how the broader engineering org works</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement monitoring, logging, and observability solutions using CloudWatch, DataDog, and other tooling to ensure system health and performance are visible and actionable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automate security scanning, vulnerability assessments, and compliance checks within CI/CD pipelines, closing the gap between \"we run scans\" and \"we act on what they find\"</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure all infrastructure is managed via IaC (Terraform), so that reproducibility and version control are properties of the system rather than aspirations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect and implement deployment strategies, including blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks, with the goal of making production changes safe by default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advance software supply chain security across dependency risk, artifact integrity, and code signing, and guide implementation patterns that other engineering teams can adopt</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI-powered tools to analyze risks, identify consolidation opportunities across our estate, and generate assessment summaries that would otherwise require significant manual effort</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep infrastructure command.</strong> In your first 90 days, we would expect you to build a comprehensive understanding of our cloud environment: the services we run, how they are configured, where the risk concentrations are, and where the highest-leverage improvements sit. You are the person the team looks to for confident answers about how our infrastructure actually works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>IaC coverage and reliability.</strong> By the end of your first year, our Terraform footprint has meaningfully expanded, drift has been reduced, and the infrastructure that matters most is managed in code without exceptions. New environments and services are provisioned reproducibly rather than by hand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A stronger security and compliance posture.</strong> You have materially contributed to how we implement HIPAA, SOC 2, and ISO controls in our cloud environment. Compliance is not a periodic scramble but a set of automated checks and repeatable patterns that hold up under audit and under real-world pressure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deployment maturity.</strong> Blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks are in production for the services where they matter most. The team's default expectation for a production change is that it can be made safely and reverted quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>An AI-native infrastructure team.</strong> You have raised the bar for how the Infrastructure function uses AI, both in your own work and in your coaching of the team. Configuration, scripting, troubleshooting, and risk analysis are all being accelerated by AI in ways that are measurable, safe, and repeatable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Six or more years of experience in DevOps, Infrastructure, and Cloud Engineering, with a track record of operating at a senior technical level in production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of HIPAA, SOC-2, and ISO compliance frameworks and their technical implementation. You have translated compliance requirements into infrastructure controls</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in AWS, including EKS, RDS, Security Hub, Identity Center, and Control Tower. You are fluent in the AWS security and account management primitives, not just the compute and storage ones</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of Postgres or other relational databases, including operational responsibilities such as performance tuning, backups, and failover</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong expertise in CI/CD pipelines, particularly GitHub Actions &amp; ArgoCD, and a clear point of view on how to structure pipelines that are fast, safe, and observable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid grasp of security best practices in CI/CD pipelines and cloud infrastructure, with the practical experience to know where the common failure modes are</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), including building and managing declarative GitOps deployment patterns via ArgoCD to handle application lifecycle management at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine AI fluency in your daily infrastructure practice. You use AI tools daily to accelerate IaC, scripting, and troubleshooting. Rather than relying on AI as an occasional aid, you understand how to structure configurations so AI agents can reliably consume them, and you actively evaluate the security and quality of AI-generated code. Candidates who treat AI as a novelty rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced knowledge of Cloudflare and its role in edge, security, and performance architectures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex deployment issues under production pressure without losing composure or accuracy</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>AI REQUIREMENTS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. To be successful at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $165,000 - $185,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Senior DevOps Engineer at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com's infrastructure is the layer on which everything else depends. Our marketplace, integrations, data warehouse, and clinical workflows all run on a cloud environment that must be reliable, observable, secure, and compliant with the frameworks governing healthcare technology. As we scale, that layer needs to scale with us, and the engineering practices around it need to mature at the same pace.\n\nWe are seeking a Senior DevOps Engineer to join our Infrastructure team as we expand the DevOps function. This is a hands-on senior role that combines deep technical execution with the kind of engineering judgment that shapes how a growing infrastructure team operates. You will report into our Infrastructure leadership and work closely with Engineering, Security, and Compliance across a HIPAA-regulated environment.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Provide hands-on DevOps work across the network, servers, and cloud platforms, operating as a senior technical contributor from day one\n\n - Ensure DevOps and Engineering processes align with security best practices, and help embed those practices deeper into how the broader engineering org works\n\n - Implement monitoring, logging, and observability solutions using CloudWatch, DataDog, and other tooling to ensure system health and performance are visible and actionable\n\n - Automate security scanning, vulnerability assessments, and compliance checks within CI/CD pipelines, closing the gap between \"we run scans\" and \"we act on what they find\"\n\n - Ensure all infrastructure is managed via IaC (Terraform), so that reproducibility and version control are properties of the system rather than aspirations\n\n - Architect and implement deployment strategies, including blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks, with the goal of making production changes safe by default\n\n - Advance software supply chain security across dependency risk, artifact integrity, and code signing, and guide implementation patterns that other engineering teams can adopt\n\n - Leverage AI-powered tools to analyze risks, identify consolidation opportunities across our estate, and generate assessment summaries that would otherwise require significant manual effort\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE\n\n 1. Deep infrastructure command. In your first 90 days, we would expect you to build a comprehensive understanding of our cloud environment: the services we run, how they are configured, where the risk concentrations are, and where the highest-leverage improvements sit. You are the person the team looks to for confident answers about how our infrastructure actually works.\n\n 2. IaC coverage and reliability. By the end of your first year, our Terraform footprint has meaningfully expanded, drift has been reduced, and the infrastructure that matters most is managed in code without exceptions. New environments and services are provisioned reproducibly rather than by hand.\n\n 3. A stronger security and compliance posture. You have materially contributed to how we implement HIPAA, SOC 2, and ISO controls in our cloud environment. Compliance is not a periodic scramble but a set of automated checks and repeatable patterns that hold up under audit and under real-world pressure.\n\n 4. Deployment maturity. Blue-green deployments, canary releases, and automated rollbacks are in production for the services where they matter most. The team's default expectation for a production change is that it can be made safely and reverted quickly.\n\n 5. An AI-native infrastructure team. You have raised the bar for how the Infrastructure function uses AI, both in your own work and in your coaching of the team. Configuration, scripting, troubleshooting, and risk analysis are all being accelerated by AI in ways that are measurable, safe, and repeatable.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Six or more years of experience in DevOps, Infrastructure, and Cloud Engineering, with a track record of operating at a senior technical level in production environments\n\n - Deep understanding of HIPAA, SOC-2, and ISO compliance frameworks and their technical implementation. You have translated compliance requirements into infrastructure controls\n\n - Expertise in AWS, including EKS, RDS, Security Hub, Identity Center, and Control Tower. You are fluent in the AWS security and account management primitives, not just the compute and storage ones\n\n - Strong working knowledge of Postgres or other relational databases, including operational responsibilities such as performance tuning, backups, and failover\n\n - Strong expertise in CI/CD pipelines, particularly GitHub Actions & ArgoCD, and a clear point of view on how to structure pipelines that are fast, safe, and observable\n\n - Solid grasp of security best practices in CI/CD pipelines and cloud infrastructure, with the practical experience to know where the common failure modes are\n\n - Hands-on experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), including building and managing declarative GitOps deployment patterns via ArgoCD to handle application lifecycle management at scale\n\n - Genuine AI fluency in your daily infrastructure practice. You use AI tools daily to accelerate IaC, scripting, and troubleshooting. Rather than relying on AI as an occasional aid, you understand how to structure configurations so AI agents can reliably consume them, and you actively evaluate the security and quality of AI-generated code. Candidates who treat AI as a novelty rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this role\n\n - Advanced knowledge of Cloudflare and its role in edge, security, and performance architectures\n\n - Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex deployment issues under production pressure without losing composure or accuracy\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)\n   \n   - You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.\n   \n   - You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.\n   \n   - You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.\n   \n   - Assessment: a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. To be successful at Scan.com http://Scan.com, you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $165,000 - $185,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$140K – $175K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$140K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"b0c8345d-e3d5-4427-bcc4-7c8b29f0cdb4","tierSummary":"$140K – $175K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"7e9eaf68-4b45-4613-ae68-5aaaf120ecf7","summary":"$140K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":175000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":175000}]}},{"id":"22029304-fee2-40f1-9c10-4f61347749ac","title":"MRI Technologist, Chicago Southland","department":"Operations (US)","team":"Operations (US)","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T15:15:18.847+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Georgia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Atlanta"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/22029304-fee2-40f1-9c10-4f61347749ac","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/22029304-fee2-40f1-9c10-4f61347749ac/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Mobile MRI Technologist</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Mobile MRI Technologist</strong>, you are the clinical heartbeat of our physical operations. Reporting to the Director of Imaging Performance, you will lead the day-to-day clinical functions of our high-end mobile units. Unlike traditional \"traveling\" roles, our units are permanently parked, providing a stable home base for you to deliver exceptional care. You will be responsible for the end-to-end patient experience, from safety screening to high-fidelity imaging, while ensuring our facilities meet the gold standard of ACR compliance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Precision:</strong> Executing high-quality MRI scans with a focus on diagnostic excellence and patient comfort.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Care:</strong> Provide compassionate, patient-centered care by explaining MRI procedures, addressing concerns, and ensuring patient comfort and safety throughout imaging exams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>System Management:</strong> Taking full \"ownership\" of our Siemens Espree systems, ensuring the system performs at peak levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Quality Assurance:</strong> Managing documentation of daily QC/QA procedures required for safety and accreditation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Advocacy:</strong> Leading patient screening and safety protocols to ensure a seamless, anxiety-free experience for every visitor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Troubleshooting:</strong> Acting as the first line of defense for the unit by identifying equipment issues and collaborating with Field Service Engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Workflow Optimization:</strong> Utilizing Acuity Scheduling and Google Workspace to manage patient flow and maintain digital records.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Autonomy:</strong> Establish yourself as the trusted lead for your site, managing full-day scan schedules with zero-to-minimal oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ACR Gold Standard:</strong> Successfully lead or maintain the ACR certification process for your mobile unit, ensuring 100% compliance with safety standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Fluidity:</strong> Master Acuity and Google Workspace to ensure all patient documentation is 100% accurate and submitted in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Zero Downtime Mentality:</strong> Develop a proactive maintenance relationship with Field Service Engineers, identifying and flagging potential system issues before they impact the patient schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Satisfaction:</strong> Maintain a high patient NPS (Net Promoter Score) by delivering a \"concierge-style\" imaging experience that aligns with the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> mission.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">These might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Accreditation:</strong> You hold a current ARRT (MR) credential.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Expertise:</strong> You have extensive experience specifically navigating and scanning on Siemens Espree MRI systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compliance Knowledge:</strong> You have a proven track record of obtaining or maintaining ACR certification for MRI facilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Safety First:</strong> You have a deep understanding of MRI safety protocols and rigorous screening procedures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problem-Solving Skills:</strong> You are comfortable troubleshooting technical issues and communicating effectively with engineers and stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Digital Literacy:</strong> You are proficient with Google Workspace (Docs/Sheets) and are a quick study when it comes to scheduling software like Acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location Specifics:</strong> You are comfortable working in Humboldt Park.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Note: For Chicago, a dedicated parking spot is provided one block from the site.</em></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 3 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Aware. You lead with subject matter expertise, but you're comfortable using AI for things like admin, documentation, or research, so you can spend more time with patients—and you know where AI stops, and human judgment has to take over. (clinical, hands-on, and highly regulated roles where hands-on expertise is the core value)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $95,000 - $120,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Mobile MRI Technologist at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nAs a Mobile MRI Technologist, you are the clinical heartbeat of our physical operations. Reporting to the Director of Imaging Performance, you will lead the day-to-day clinical functions of our high-end mobile units. Unlike traditional \"traveling\" roles, our units are permanently parked, providing a stable home base for you to deliver exceptional care. You will be responsible for the end-to-end patient experience, from safety screening to high-fidelity imaging, while ensuring our facilities meet the gold standard of ACR compliance.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n\n\n - Clinical Precision: Executing high-quality MRI scans with a focus on diagnostic excellence and patient comfort.\n\n - Patient Care: Provide compassionate, patient-centered care by explaining MRI procedures, addressing concerns, and ensuring patient comfort and safety throughout imaging exams.\n\n - System Management: Taking full \"ownership\" of our Siemens Espree systems, ensuring the system performs at peak levels.\n\n - Quality Assurance: Managing documentation of daily QC/QA procedures required for safety and accreditation.\n\n - Patient Advocacy: Leading patient screening and safety protocols to ensure a seamless, anxiety-free experience for every visitor.\n\n - Technical Troubleshooting: Acting as the first line of defense for the unit by identifying equipment issues and collaborating with Field Service Engineers.\n\n - Workflow Optimization: Utilizing Acuity Scheduling and Google Workspace to manage patient flow and maintain digital records.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE\n\n 1. Clinical Autonomy: Establish yourself as the trusted lead for your site, managing full-day scan schedules with zero-to-minimal oversight.\n\n 2. ACR Gold Standard: Successfully lead or maintain the ACR certification process for your mobile unit, ensuring 100% compliance with safety standards.\n\n 3. Operational Fluidity: Master Acuity and Google Workspace to ensure all patient documentation is 100% accurate and submitted in real time.\n\n 4. Zero Downtime Mentality: Develop a proactive maintenance relationship with Field Service Engineers, identifying and flagging potential system issues before they impact the patient schedule.\n\n 5. Patient Satisfaction: Maintain a high patient NPS (Net Promoter Score) by delivering a \"concierge-style\" imaging experience that aligns with the Scan.com http://Scan.com mission.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nThese might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Accreditation: You hold a current ARRT (MR) credential.\n\n - Technical Expertise: You have extensive experience specifically navigating and scanning on Siemens Espree MRI systems.\n\n - Compliance Knowledge: You have a proven track record of obtaining or maintaining ACR certification for MRI facilities.\n\n - Safety First: You have a deep understanding of MRI safety protocols and rigorous screening procedures.\n\n - Problem-Solving Skills: You are comfortable troubleshooting technical issues and communicating effectively with engineers and stakeholders.\n\n - Digital Literacy: You are proficient with Google Workspace (Docs/Sheets) and are a quick study when it comes to scheduling software like Acuity.\n\n - Location Specifics: You are comfortable working in Humboldt Park.\n   \n   - Note: For Chicago, a dedicated parking spot is provided one block from the site.\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 3 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Aware. You lead with subject matter expertise, but you're comfortable using AI for things like admin, documentation, or research, so you can spend more time with patients—and you know where AI stops, and human judgment has to take over. (clinical, hands-on, and highly regulated roles where hands-on expertise is the core value)\n   \n   - Assessment: A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $95,000 - $120,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f261e903-e469-4f33-8e64-0f0233056d03","title":"MRI Technologist, Sacramento","department":"Operations (US)","team":"Operations (US)","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-28T15:25:38.695+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Georgia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Atlanta"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/f261e903-e469-4f33-8e64-0f0233056d03","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/f261e903-e469-4f33-8e64-0f0233056d03/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Mobile MRI Technologist</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Mobile MRI Technologist</strong>, you are the clinical heartbeat of our physical operations. Reporting to the Director of Imaging Performance, you will lead the day-to-day clinical functions of our high-end mobile units. Unlike traditional \"traveling\" roles, our units are permanently parked, providing a stable home base for you to deliver exceptional care. You will be responsible for the end-to-end patient experience, from safety screening to high-fidelity imaging, while ensuring our facilities meet the gold standard of ACR compliance.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Precision:</strong> Executing high-quality MRI scans with a focus on diagnostic excellence and patient comfort.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Care:</strong> Provide compassionate, patient-centered care by explaining MRI procedures, addressing concerns, and ensuring patient comfort and safety throughout imaging exams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>System Management:</strong> Taking full \"ownership\" of our Siemens Espree systems, ensuring the system performs at peak levels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Quality Assurance:</strong> Managing documentation of daily QC/QA procedures required for safety and accreditation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Advocacy:</strong> Leading patient screening and safety protocols to ensure a seamless, anxiety-free experience for every visitor.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Troubleshooting:</strong> Acting as the first line of defense for the unit by identifying equipment issues and collaborating with Field Service Engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Workflow Optimization:</strong> Utilizing Acuity Scheduling and Google Workspace to manage patient flow and maintain digital records.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Autonomy:</strong> Establish yourself as the trusted lead for your site, managing full-day scan schedules with zero-to-minimal oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ACR Gold Standard:</strong> Successfully lead or maintain the ACR certification process for your mobile unit, ensuring 100% compliance with safety standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Fluidity:</strong> Master Acuity and Google Workspace to ensure all patient documentation is 100% accurate and submitted in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Zero Downtime Mentality:</strong> Develop a proactive maintenance relationship with Field Service Engineers, identifying and flagging potential system issues before they impact the patient schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Patient Satisfaction:</strong> Maintain a high patient NPS (Net Promoter Score) by delivering a \"concierge-style\" imaging experience that aligns with the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> mission.</p></li></ol><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">These might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Accreditation:</strong> You hold a current ARRT (MR) credential.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Expertise:</strong> You have extensive experience specifically navigating and scanning on Siemens Espree MRI systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compliance Knowledge:</strong> You have a proven track record of obtaining or maintaining ACR certification for MRI facilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Safety First:</strong> You have a deep understanding of MRI safety protocols and rigorous screening procedures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problem-Solving Skills:</strong> You are comfortable troubleshooting technical issues and communicating effectively with engineers and stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Digital Literacy:</strong> You are proficient with Google Workspace (Docs/Sheets) and are a quick study when it comes to scheduling software like Acuity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location Specifics:</strong> You are comfortable working in <strong>Sacramento, CA</strong>.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 3 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Aware. You lead with subject matter expertise, but you're comfortable using AI for things like admin, documentation, or research, so you can spend more time with patients—and you know where AI stops, and human judgment has to take over. (clinical, hands-on, and highly regulated roles where hands-on expertise is the core value)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p></li></ol><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $115,000 - $145,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Mobile MRI Technologist at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nAs a Mobile MRI Technologist, you are the clinical heartbeat of our physical operations. Reporting to the Director of Imaging Performance, you will lead the day-to-day clinical functions of our high-end mobile units. Unlike traditional \"traveling\" roles, our units are permanently parked, providing a stable home base for you to deliver exceptional care. You will be responsible for the end-to-end patient experience, from safety screening to high-fidelity imaging, while ensuring our facilities meet the gold standard of ACR compliance.\n\n \n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n \n\n - Clinical Precision: Executing high-quality MRI scans with a focus on diagnostic excellence and patient comfort.\n\n - Patient Care: Provide compassionate, patient-centered care by explaining MRI procedures, addressing concerns, and ensuring patient comfort and safety throughout imaging exams.\n\n - System Management: Taking full \"ownership\" of our Siemens Espree systems, ensuring the system performs at peak levels.\n\n - Quality Assurance: Managing documentation of daily QC/QA procedures required for safety and accreditation.\n\n - Patient Advocacy: Leading patient screening and safety protocols to ensure a seamless, anxiety-free experience for every visitor.\n\n - Technical Troubleshooting: Acting as the first line of defense for the unit by identifying equipment issues and collaborating with Field Service Engineers.\n\n - Workflow Optimization: Utilizing Acuity Scheduling and Google Workspace to manage patient flow and maintain digital records.\n\n \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE\n\n 1. Clinical Autonomy: Establish yourself as the trusted lead for your site, managing full-day scan schedules with zero-to-minimal oversight.\n\n 2. ACR Gold Standard: Successfully lead or maintain the ACR certification process for your mobile unit, ensuring 100% compliance with safety standards.\n\n 3. Operational Fluidity: Master Acuity and Google Workspace to ensure all patient documentation is 100% accurate and submitted in real time.\n\n 4. Zero Downtime Mentality: Develop a proactive maintenance relationship with Field Service Engineers, identifying and flagging potential system issues before they impact the patient schedule.\n\n 5. Patient Satisfaction: Maintain a high patient NPS (Net Promoter Score) by delivering a \"concierge-style\" imaging experience that aligns with the Scan.com http://Scan.com mission.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nThese might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Accreditation: You hold a current ARRT (MR) credential.\n\n - Technical Expertise: You have extensive experience specifically navigating and scanning on Siemens Espree MRI systems.\n\n - Compliance Knowledge: You have a proven track record of obtaining or maintaining ACR certification for MRI facilities.\n\n - Safety First: You have a deep understanding of MRI safety protocols and rigorous screening procedures.\n\n - Problem-Solving Skills: You are comfortable troubleshooting technical issues and communicating effectively with engineers and stakeholders.\n\n - Digital Literacy: You are proficient with Google Workspace (Docs/Sheets) and are a quick study when it comes to scheduling software like Acuity.\n\n - Location Specifics: You are comfortable working in Sacramento, CA.\n\n \n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 3 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Aware. You lead with subject matter expertise, but you're comfortable using AI for things like admin, documentation, or research, so you can spend more time with patients—and you know where AI stops, and human judgment has to take over. (clinical, hands-on, and highly regulated roles where hands-on expertise is the core value)\n   \n   - Assessment: A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n \n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n \n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n\n \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $115,000 - $145,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cb7007ae-d7c4-4d45-ba70-6333fc162370","title":"Head of Partnerships","department":"Sales and Partnerships (UK)","team":"Sales and Partnerships (UK)","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"London Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T11:29:22.481+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Greater London","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"London"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/cb7007ae-d7c4-4d45-ba70-6333fc162370","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/cb7007ae-d7c4-4d45-ba70-6333fc162370/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Head of Partnerships</strong> to lead our UK partnerships function at an exciting time — our B2B platform is expanding rapidly across insurance, medico-legal, dental, and consultant verticals, we're now offering 10+ scan types, and working with 200+ UK imaging centres. We've raised a total of $100m in VC funding, reached profitability, and have a 100%+ yearly growth trajectory.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a commercial role reporting directly to the UK Managing Director, based in London. You'll lead the Business Development function and shape its structure, owning the UK partnerships pipeline end-to-end — from field-based outreach through to commercial negotiation and close. Working cross-functionally with our operations, product and clinical teams, you'll be the face of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> for our most important clients — building trust, driving performance, and identifying new opportunities to grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an early-stage business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and managing a pipeline of B2B partnership opportunities across insurers, cash-plan providers, dental groups, referring provider practices, and healthcare networks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Getting out in the field — calling on and visiting referring provider practices directly to bring them onto the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leading commercial negotiations from initial outreach through to contract signature, and meeting targets for sign-ups and referral volume</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Setting and owning the partnerships strategy for the UK business, in collaboration with the MD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintaining relationships with existing partners, sharing feedback and market insight back into the wider <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> team to shape strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working cross-functionally with product, supply, and finance teams — including colleagues in the US — to structure deals that work operationally as well as commercially</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Representing <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> at industry events and building the company's profile in the UK healthcare partnerships landscape</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE:</h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and convert a qualified partnerships pipeline, closing several anchor B2B deals across priority verticals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a clear, repeatable framework for sourcing, negotiating, and closing partnership deals — including field-based referral outreach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow revenue and volume from existing key accounts through renegotiated or expanded terms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong, trusted relationships with senior stakeholders across partner organisations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a collaborative, values-led member of the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> team — bringing energy, curiosity, and a solutions-first mindset to everything you do</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth role, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong track record in B2B partnerships, field sales, or commercial negotiation, ideally in healthcare, health tech, or a related regulated industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience in a closing sales role, with confidence in cold-calling and dropping into potential clients unannounced</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidence leading complex negotiations and closing deals with senior stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A self-starter approach — comfortable building a pipeline from scratch and working autonomously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial acumen and the ability to think strategically about market positioning and growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly across clinical, operational, and commercial audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a fast-paced, scaling business where priorities can shift</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel across the UK — a full, clean driving licence is helpful</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Talent Partner. The call is usually via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a 45-minute video call with the hiring manager. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All of our roles will have a small assessment stage. This might be in person, a take-home assessment or further video calls. Length varies, but we're mindful of your time and try to keep it as simple as possible.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, the length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2>BENEFITS:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of £70,000 – £80,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory pension</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment needed for you to do your role effectively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible working</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personal Development budgets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28 days of annual leave plus bank holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Wellness budget to spend via a partner platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to talking therapy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Head of Partnerships to lead our UK partnerships function at an exciting time — our B2B platform is expanding rapidly across insurance, medico-legal, dental, and consultant verticals, we're now offering 10+ scan types, and working with 200+ UK imaging centres. We've raised a total of $100m in VC funding, reached profitability, and have a 100%+ yearly growth trajectory.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN:\n\nThis is a commercial role reporting directly to the UK Managing Director, based in London. You'll lead the Business Development function and shape its structure, owning the UK partnerships pipeline end-to-end — from field-based outreach through to commercial negotiation and close. Working cross-functionally with our operations, product and clinical teams, you'll be the face of Scan.com http://Scan.com for our most important clients — building trust, driving performance, and identifying new opportunities to grow.\n\n\n\nAs an early-stage business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Building and managing a pipeline of B2B partnership opportunities across insurers, cash-plan providers, dental groups, referring provider practices, and healthcare networks\n\n - Getting out in the field — calling on and visiting referring provider practices directly to bring them onto the Scan.com http://Scan.com platform\n\n - Leading commercial negotiations from initial outreach through to contract signature, and meeting targets for sign-ups and referral volume\n\n - Setting and owning the partnerships strategy for the UK business, in collaboration with the MD\n\n - Maintaining relationships with existing partners, sharing feedback and market insight back into the wider Scan.com http://Scan.com team to shape strategy\n\n - Working cross-functionally with product, supply, and finance teams — including colleagues in the US — to structure deals that work operationally as well as commercially\n\n - Representing Scan.com http://Scan.com at industry events and building the company's profile in the UK healthcare partnerships landscape\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE:\n\n 1. Build and convert a qualified partnerships pipeline, closing several anchor B2B deals across priority verticals\n\n 2. Establish a clear, repeatable framework for sourcing, negotiating, and closing partnership deals — including field-based referral outreach\n\n 3. Grow revenue and volume from existing key accounts through renegotiated or expanded terms\n\n 4. Build strong, trusted relationships with senior stakeholders across partner organisations\n\n 5. Be a collaborative, values-led member of the Scan.com http://Scan.com team — bringing energy, curiosity, and a solutions-first mindset to everything you do\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE:\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth role, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - A strong track record in B2B partnerships, field sales, or commercial negotiation, ideally in healthcare, health tech, or a related regulated industry\n\n - Proven experience in a closing sales role, with confidence in cold-calling and dropping into potential clients unannounced\n\n - Confidence leading complex negotiations and closing deals with senior stakeholders\n\n - A self-starter approach — comfortable building a pipeline from scratch and working autonomously\n\n - Strong commercial acumen and the ability to think strategically about market positioning and growth\n\n - Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly across clinical, operational, and commercial audiences\n\n - Comfortable working in a fast-paced, scaling business where priorities can shift\n\n - Willingness to travel across the UK — a full, clean driving licence is helpful\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU:\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Talent Partner. The call is usually via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a 45-minute video call with the hiring manager. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. All of our roles will have a small assessment stage. This might be in person, a take-home assessment or further video calls. Length varies, but we're mindful of your time and try to keep it as simple as possible.\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, the length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n    \n    \n\n\nBENEFITS:\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of £70,000 – £80,000\n\n - Statutory pension\n\n - Healthcare plan\n\n - All the equipment needed for you to do your role effectively\n\n - Flexible working\n\n - Personal Development budgets\n\n - 28 days of annual leave plus bank holidays\n\n - Wellness budget to spend via a partner platform\n\n - Access to talking therapy\n\n - Inclusive policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7c578bb2-563d-4ad4-80c1-020e8134de86","title":"Software Engineer, Integrations","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-16T20:08:54.851+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/7c578bb2-563d-4ad4-80c1-020e8134de86","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/7c578bb2-563d-4ad4-80c1-020e8134de86/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Software Engineer, Integrations, </strong>at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.<br /></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>'s integration layer is mission-critical infrastructure. We interface with hundreds of imaging centers and health systems operating disparate, often decades-old systems — RIS platforms built on legacy protocols, HL7 v2 feeds with idiosyncratic vendor dialects, and hardware gateways running in constrained clinical environments. On the demand side, we connect to modern EHR APIs, third-party referral networks, and portal integrations that must work reliably at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Software Engineer, Integrations</strong>, you will architect and build the systems that make the demand-side connections robust, observable, and extensible. This problem area requires genuine passion for system integration patterns, message transformation pipelines, and the operational discipline to maintain high-reliability infrastructure in the face of real-world entropy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain integration connectors for modern and legacy EHR systems to retrieve physician referrals and relevant patient documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect a fault-tolerant message queuing and delivery infrastructure for inbound and outbound HL7 and API traffic.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain REST API integrations with third-party referral sources, attorney platforms, and demand aggregators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the observability layer for the integration infrastructure: structured logging, alerting on message processing latency/failures, and dashboards that surface issues before they reach the operations teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep domain ownership.</strong> Within 90 days, you have a complete mental model of our integration workflows — every active connector, its transport mechanism, its failure modes, and its monitoring coverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resilience uplift.</strong> You have identified and remediated the most critical reliability gaps in our referral pipeline. There is a measurable reduction in integration-related operational escalations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Scalable transformation architecture.</strong> You have designed or materially evolved our data workflows such that onboarding a new demand-side source is a simple choice from a menu of robust technical options.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Observability in production.</strong> Every integration has structured alerting and a clear SLA. The operations team can self-serve integration health for routine issues without engineering involvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shipped meaningful capability.</strong> At least two significant referral integration improvements. This can be new connectors that significantly increase referral volume, automations that improve quality, or infrastructure improvements. These improvements are live in production and have measurably increased referral volume, improved connection optionality, operational efficiency, and reduced error rates.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to integrate with legacy systems that were not designed for modern interoperability. For example, aging RIS platforms in radiology, core banking systems in fintech, or equivalent legacy infrastructure in another vertical. The underlying pattern of bridging old and new matters more than the specific domain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one backend language used in high-reliability integration contexts (Python, Ruby, Java, C# are all relevant; language is less important than architectural rigor).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with RESTful API integration patterns, including schema versioning, backward compatibility, and API contract management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational instincts: you instrument what you build, you think about failure modes before they happen, and you treat on-call escalations as a signal about systemic gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias for innovation: You care about questioning the ‘why’ behind every system, and have a strong desire to build the next generation of products you work on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare is a plus, but not required. We care far more about your engineering depth and API design fluency than your industry background</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done because of it.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>OUR VALUES</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $180,000 - $220,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Software Engineer, Integrations, at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com's integration layer is mission-critical infrastructure. We interface with hundreds of imaging centers and health systems operating disparate, often decades-old systems — RIS platforms built on legacy protocols, HL7 v2 feeds with idiosyncratic vendor dialects, and hardware gateways running in constrained clinical environments. On the demand side, we connect to modern EHR APIs, third-party referral networks, and portal integrations that must work reliably at scale.\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Integrations, you will architect and build the systems that make the demand-side connections robust, observable, and extensible. This problem area requires genuine passion for system integration patterns, message transformation pipelines, and the operational discipline to maintain high-reliability infrastructure in the face of real-world entropy.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Build and maintain integration connectors for modern and legacy EHR systems to retrieve physician referrals and relevant patient documentation.\n\n - Architect a fault-tolerant message queuing and delivery infrastructure for inbound and outbound HL7 and API traffic.\n\n - Build and maintain REST API integrations with third-party referral sources, attorney platforms, and demand aggregators.\n\n - Own the observability layer for the integration infrastructure: structured logging, alerting on message processing latency/failures, and dashboards that surface issues before they reach the operations teams.\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR\n\n 1. Deep domain ownership. Within 90 days, you have a complete mental model of our integration workflows — every active connector, its transport mechanism, its failure modes, and its monitoring coverage.\n\n 2. Resilience uplift. You have identified and remediated the most critical reliability gaps in our referral pipeline. There is a measurable reduction in integration-related operational escalations.\n\n 3. Scalable transformation architecture. You have designed or materially evolved our data workflows such that onboarding a new demand-side source is a simple choice from a menu of robust technical options.\n\n 4. Observability in production. Every integration has structured alerting and a clear SLA. The operations team can self-serve integration health for routine issues without engineering involvement.\n\n 5. Shipped meaningful capability. At least two significant referral integration improvements. This can be new connectors that significantly increase referral volume, automations that improve quality, or infrastructure improvements. These improvements are live in production and have measurably increased referral volume, improved connection optionality, operational efficiency, and reduced error rates.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Proven ability to integrate with legacy systems that were not designed for modern interoperability. For example, aging RIS platforms in radiology, core banking systems in fintech, or equivalent legacy infrastructure in another vertical. The underlying pattern of bridging old and new matters more than the specific domain.\n\n - Proficiency in at least one backend language used in high-reliability integration contexts (Python, Ruby, Java, C# are all relevant; language is less important than architectural rigor).\n\n - Familiarity with RESTful API integration patterns, including schema versioning, backward compatibility, and API contract management\n\n - Strong operational instincts: you instrument what you build, you think about failure modes before they happen, and you treat on-call escalations as a signal about systemic gaps\n\n - Bias for innovation: You care about questioning the ‘why’ behind every system, and have a strong desire to build the next generation of products you work on.\n\n - Experience in healthcare is a plus, but not required. We care far more about your engineering depth and API design fluency than your industry background\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done because of it.\n\n - Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)\n   \n   - You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.\n   \n   - You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.\n   \n   - You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.\n   \n   - Assessment: a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $180,000 - $220,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $160K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"a5bdc70a-9c0e-4327-a47d-cfddfe37b3b6","tierSummary":"$100K – $160K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"84c34f7d-c046-4aba-a4f1-e8164f5d7d6b","summary":"$100K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":160000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":160000}]}},{"id":"ad89c3a6-31de-47e7-9204-5ac516130cc7","title":"Software Engineer, Fulfillment","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-20T15:19:20.077+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/ad89c3a6-31de-47e7-9204-5ac516130cc7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/ad89c3a6-31de-47e7-9204-5ac516130cc7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Software Engineer, Fulfillment</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>'s Fulfillment product is the company's core engine. We use an internal portal that manages the entire patient lifecycle, from referral receipt to radiology reports sent. With it, we are able to schedule patients, assess patient preauthorization, handle medical forms, send notifications, route images and reports, generate invoices &amp; claims — all connected to hundreds of imaging centers and health systems operating disparate, often decades-old systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Software Engineer, Fulfillment, you will architect and build the systems that make these workflows robust, automated, and efficient. This problem area requires genuine passion for scaling operational workflows, working collaboratively with internal operations teams, and the discipline to understand the ins and outs of high-throughput workflows. The reality is that we help hundreds of patients get imaging done every day, and our team is passionate about making sure folks get their care with little to no friction.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement patient intake workflows. This includes finishing medical forms, scheduling appointments, and receiving relevant reminders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect a monitoring system of patients in their journey at scale for operations leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop delightful, efficient dashboards for scheduling, legal operations, and patient services team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the automation layer for the operations team: automatic referral ingestion, automatic task assignment, AI voice reminder calls, and dashboards that surface issues to operational leads before they affect patient service expectations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR:</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Deep domain ownership.</strong> Within 60 days, you have a complete mental model of our patient journey — every status, every trigger for status change, every role and their tasks, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Resilience uplift.</strong> You have identified and remediated the most critical workflows for our internal products. There is a measurable reduction in workflow-related operational escalations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Simplicity by design.</strong> You have designed or materially evolved our workflows such that a new operations team member can start working with little to no training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turnaround time reduction.</strong> Your work has significantly improved our end-to-end turnaround times for scheduling patients and returning reports to referring providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-enabled scale.</strong> You have shipped improvements that drastically reduce the time each operational team member spends serving patients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to integrate with legacy systems that were not designed for modern interoperability. For example, aging RIS platforms in radiology, core banking systems in fintech, or equivalent legacy infrastructure in another vertical. The underlying pattern of bridging old and new matters more than the specific domain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with shipping complex internal operations dashboards and creating delightful experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in backend development within modern web stacks—particularly Ruby (e.g., Rails) with an emphasis on building reliable, scalable services and maintaining architectural rigor over specific language choice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with RESTful API integration patterns, including schema versioning, backward compatibility, and API contract management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong operational instincts: you instrument what you build, you think about failure modes before they happen, and you treat on-call escalations as a signal about systemic gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare is a plus, but not required. We care far more about your engineering depth and legacy system fluency than your industry background</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order depending on team availability:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory video call with our Senior Talent Partner, approximately 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Video call with a software engineer on the team, approximately 60 minutes. This will be a live assessment of your technical skill.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assessment stage, which may be a take-home exercise, in-person session, or a combination of the two.This will be cross functional in nature, and will assess your systems design skills along with your ability to evolve a feature with your future teammates. We will be mindful of your time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Final round with our Chief Technology Officer and Chief Product Officer. This round will assess alignment with our company values.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>BENEFITS:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $170,000 - $220,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare, Vision, and Dental</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All equipment needed to do your role effectively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible and remote/hybrid working options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personal development budgets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">18 days PTO plus public holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10 paid sick days</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Software Engineer, Fulfillment at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN:\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com's Fulfillment product is the company's core engine. We use an internal portal that manages the entire patient lifecycle, from referral receipt to radiology reports sent. With it, we are able to schedule patients, assess patient preauthorization, handle medical forms, send notifications, route images and reports, generate invoices & claims — all connected to hundreds of imaging centers and health systems operating disparate, often decades-old systems.\n\nAs a Software Engineer, Fulfillment, you will architect and build the systems that make these workflows robust, automated, and efficient. This problem area requires genuine passion for scaling operational workflows, working collaboratively with internal operations teams, and the discipline to understand the ins and outs of high-throughput workflows. The reality is that we help hundreds of patients get imaging done every day, and our team is passionate about making sure folks get their care with little to no friction.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Design and implement patient intake workflows. This includes finishing medical forms, scheduling appointments, and receiving relevant reminders.\n\n - Architect a monitoring system of patients in their journey at scale for operations leadership.\n\n - Develop delightful, efficient dashboards for scheduling, legal operations, and patient services team members.\n\n - Own the automation layer for the operations team: automatic referral ingestion, automatic task assignment, AI voice reminder calls, and dashboards that surface issues to operational leads before they affect patient service expectations.\n\n\n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR:\n\n 1. Deep domain ownership. Within 60 days, you have a complete mental model of our patient journey — every status, every trigger for status change, every role and their tasks, etc.\n\n 2. Resilience uplift. You have identified and remediated the most critical workflows for our internal products. There is a measurable reduction in workflow-related operational escalations.\n\n 3. Simplicity by design. You have designed or materially evolved our workflows such that a new operations team member can start working with little to no training.\n\n 4. Turnaround time reduction. Your work has significantly improved our end-to-end turnaround times for scheduling patients and returning reports to referring providers.\n\n 5. AI-enabled scale. You have shipped improvements that drastically reduce the time each operational team member spends serving patients.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE:\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n\n\n - Proven ability to integrate with legacy systems that were not designed for modern interoperability. For example, aging RIS platforms in radiology, core banking systems in fintech, or equivalent legacy infrastructure in another vertical. The underlying pattern of bridging old and new matters more than the specific domain.\n\n - Experience with shipping complex internal operations dashboards and creating delightful experiences.\n\n - Proficiency in backend development within modern web stacks—particularly Ruby (e.g., Rails) with an emphasis on building reliable, scalable services and maintaining architectural rigor over specific language choice.\n\n - Familiarity with RESTful API integration patterns, including schema versioning, backward compatibility, and API contract management\n\n - Strong operational instincts: you instrument what you build, you think about failure modes before they happen, and you treat on-call escalations as a signal about systemic gaps\n\n - Experience in healthcare is a plus, but not required. We care far more about your engineering depth and legacy system fluency than your industry background\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU:\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order depending on team availability:\n\n - Introductory video call with our Senior Talent Partner, approximately 30 minutes.\n\n - Video call with a software engineer on the team, approximately 60 minutes. This will be a live assessment of your technical skill.\n\n - Assessment stage, which may be a take-home exercise, in-person session, or a combination of the two.This will be cross functional in nature, and will assess your systems design skills along with your ability to evolve a feature with your future teammates. We will be mindful of your time.\n\n - Final round with our Chief Technology Officer and Chief Product Officer. This round will assess alignment with our company values.\n\n - Offer!\n   \n   \n\n\nBENEFITS:\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $170,000 - $220,000\n\n - 401k\n\n - Healthcare, Vision, and Dental\n\n - All equipment needed to do your role effectively\n\n - Flexible and remote/hybrid working options\n\n - Personal development budgets\n\n - 18 days PTO plus public holidays\n\n - 10 paid sick days\n\n - Inclusive policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $140K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"01dd5c39-8f37-47fb-b158-8ff617dea389","tierSummary":"$100K – $140K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ed684931-1a28-434f-856a-a7371dfd8dc6","summary":"$100K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":140000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":140000}]}},{"id":"9e9e2b43-defd-4444-a469-5b79333e969d","title":"Senior Engineering Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-20T18:14:06.532+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/9e9e2b43-defd-4444-a469-5b79333e969d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/9e9e2b43-defd-4444-a469-5b79333e969d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Senior Engineering Manager</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a small, high-output team building across a complex technical surface: consumer marketplace, provider-facing scheduling tools, interoperability infrastructure, revenue cycle tooling, and AI-augmented workflows. We don't scale headcount to scale output. We scale leverage through AI-native development practices, tight feedback loops, and engineers who own outcomes rather than tickets.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As <strong>Senior Engineering Manager</strong>, you will lead a cross-functional engineering team and remain a hands-on contributor. We expect roughly 30% of your time to be spent writing code, reviewing architecture, or directly shaping technical decisions. This is not a role for someone who wants to move fully into management. It's a role for someone who finds that combination energising.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will report to our CTO and partner closely with Product, Operations, and Data to ship the systems that run our business. You are expected to be genuinely AI-native: not just comfortable with AI tooling, but actively shaping how your team uses it. That means deploying agents, building evaluation frameworks, and coaching engineers to work at a level of throughput that wasn't possible two years ago.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and develop a team of engineers across multiple product domains, owning velocity, process, performance, technical growth, and team culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remain a consistent technical contributor by writing production code, leading design reviews, and pairing with engineers on complex problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and enforce engineering standards across code quality, system design, testing discipline, deployment practices, and incident response</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive the team's AI-native operating model by identifying where AI agents can replace or accelerate engineering workflows, building evaluation frameworks to measure output quality, and coaching engineers to leverage AI tooling as a primary development instrument rather than an occasional aid</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product to refine roadmaps, push back on scope where necessary, and ensure the team is working on the highest-leverage problems at any given time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the architecture of your team's systems by making build vs. buy decisions, managing technical debt deliberately, and ensuring the stack can support the growth trajectory of the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>'s broader engineering culture through interview loops, cross-team design reviews, engineering all-hands, and the institutional knowledge that makes a small team punch above its weight</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team command and trust.</strong> Within 90 days, your team has a clear understanding of expectations, a functioning operating rhythm, and confidence that you are both technically credible and invested in their growth. Engineers on your team are shipping more and learning faster than before you arrived.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-native team operating model in production.</strong> You have assessed the team's current AI tooling practices, identified the highest-leverage gaps, and implemented a repeatable framework across agents, evals, and development workflows that measurably increases throughput without degrading quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical ownership.</strong> You have a complete grasp of the systems your team owns: their architecture, observability, failure modes, scalability constraints, and debt profile. You have a prioritized plan for the most critical improvements and have begun executing against it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Meaningful individual contribution.</strong> Your 30% contributor commitment is real and visible. You have shipped production code, driven at least one significant architectural decision, and demonstrated to your team that you can still do the work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Organizational trust.</strong> Product, Operations, and Data treat you as a peer. You have built the credibility to push back on scope, advocate for technical investment, and represent Engineering in cross-functional prioritization with authority. You are the go-to person for sequencing within large initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience managing and growing engineering teams in a startup environment. You have operated with limited resources, changing priorities, and a high bar for individual output, and you have thrived in that context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine AI-native fluency: you have deployed AI agents in production engineering workflows, you understand evaluation frameworks and can design them for non-trivial tasks, and you have coached teams to use AI as a primary tool rather than a novelty. Candidates who cannot speak concretely to this will not be competitive</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active technical contributor with strong engineering fundamentals. You write production-quality code in at least one modern backend or full-stack language, can lead a system design discussion at a senior level, and have not been out of the code for more than a year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a scaling healthcare technology company is a strong plus. Familiarity with the regulatory environment, interoperability constraints, and the operational complexity of healthcare delivery meaningfully shortens the ramp</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong cross-functional instincts: you have partnered effectively with Product and Operations, understand how to negotiate scope without burning relationships, and can represent technical constraints to a non-technical audience without losing fidelity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of growing engineers. ICs on your previous teams have been promoted, expanded their scope, and credited you with material development in their careers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership orientation: you do not wait to be asked, you do not manage up problems without a proposed path forward, and you treat the business outcomes of your team's work as personally yours</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here.  To be successful at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, but don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and lasts around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many interviewers, and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $180,000 - $240,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Senior Engineering Manager at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nWe are a small, high-output team building across a complex technical surface: consumer marketplace, provider-facing scheduling tools, interoperability infrastructure, revenue cycle tooling, and AI-augmented workflows. We don't scale headcount to scale output. We scale leverage through AI-native development practices, tight feedback loops, and engineers who own outcomes rather than tickets.\n\n\n\nAs Senior Engineering Manager, you will lead a cross-functional engineering team and remain a hands-on contributor. We expect roughly 30% of your time to be spent writing code, reviewing architecture, or directly shaping technical decisions. This is not a role for someone who wants to move fully into management. It's a role for someone who finds that combination energising.\n\n\n\nYou will report to our CTO and partner closely with Product, Operations, and Data to ship the systems that run our business. You are expected to be genuinely AI-native: not just comfortable with AI tooling, but actively shaping how your team uses it. That means deploying agents, building evaluation frameworks, and coaching engineers to work at a level of throughput that wasn't possible two years ago.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n\n\n - Lead and develop a team of engineers across multiple product domains, owning velocity, process, performance, technical growth, and team culture\n\n - Remain a consistent technical contributor by writing production code, leading design reviews, and pairing with engineers on complex problems.\n\n - Define and enforce engineering standards across code quality, system design, testing discipline, deployment practices, and incident response\n\n - Drive the team's AI-native operating model by identifying where AI agents can replace or accelerate engineering workflows, building evaluation frameworks to measure output quality, and coaching engineers to leverage AI tooling as a primary development instrument rather than an occasional aid\n\n - Partner with Product to refine roadmaps, push back on scope where necessary, and ensure the team is working on the highest-leverage problems at any given time\n\n - Own the architecture of your team's systems by making build vs. buy decisions, managing technical debt deliberately, and ensuring the stack can support the growth trajectory of the business\n\n - Contribute to Scan.com http://Scan.com's broader engineering culture through interview loops, cross-team design reviews, engineering all-hands, and the institutional knowledge that makes a small team punch above its weight\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR\n\n 1. Team command and trust. Within 90 days, your team has a clear understanding of expectations, a functioning operating rhythm, and confidence that you are both technically credible and invested in their growth. Engineers on your team are shipping more and learning faster than before you arrived.\n\n 2. AI-native team operating model in production. You have assessed the team's current AI tooling practices, identified the highest-leverage gaps, and implemented a repeatable framework across agents, evals, and development workflows that measurably increases throughput without degrading quality.\n\n 3. Technical ownership. You have a complete grasp of the systems your team owns: their architecture, observability, failure modes, scalability constraints, and debt profile. You have a prioritized plan for the most critical improvements and have begun executing against it.\n\n 4. Meaningful individual contribution. Your 30% contributor commitment is real and visible. You have shipped production code, driven at least one significant architectural decision, and demonstrated to your team that you can still do the work.\n\n 5. Organizational trust. Product, Operations, and Data treat you as a peer. You have built the credibility to push back on scope, advocate for technical investment, and represent Engineering in cross-functional prioritization with authority. You are the go-to person for sequencing within large initiatives.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Proven experience managing and growing engineering teams in a startup environment. You have operated with limited resources, changing priorities, and a high bar for individual output, and you have thrived in that context.\n\n - Genuine AI-native fluency: you have deployed AI agents in production engineering workflows, you understand evaluation frameworks and can design them for non-trivial tasks, and you have coached teams to use AI as a primary tool rather than a novelty. Candidates who cannot speak concretely to this will not be competitive\n\n - Active technical contributor with strong engineering fundamentals. You write production-quality code in at least one modern backend or full-stack language, can lead a system design discussion at a senior level, and have not been out of the code for more than a year\n\n - Experience in a scaling healthcare technology company is a strong plus. Familiarity with the regulatory environment, interoperability constraints, and the operational complexity of healthcare delivery meaningfully shortens the ramp\n\n - Strong cross-functional instincts: you have partnered effectively with Product and Operations, understand how to negotiate scope without burning relationships, and can represent technical constraints to a non-technical audience without losing fidelity\n\n - A track record of growing engineers. ICs on your previous teams have been promoted, expanded their scope, and credited you with material development in their careers\n\n - High ownership orientation: you do not wait to be asked, you do not manage up problems without a proposed path forward, and you treat the business outcomes of your team's work as personally yours\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)\n   \n   - You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.\n   \n   - You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.\n   \n   - You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.\n   \n   - Assessment: A practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here.  To be successful at Scan.com http://Scan.com you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, but don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and lasts around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many interviewers, and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $180,000 - $240,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$180K – $240K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$180K - $240K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1730086f-a4dc-4673-b702-0eea31a8f845","tierSummary":"$180K – $240K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"77a084cf-afff-457d-88a9-a7a79366904d","summary":"$180K – $240K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":240000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":180000,"maxValue":240000}]}},{"id":"c87f40c2-6a24-46f3-b1bc-024df1ac1106","title":"Clinical Application Administrator","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-05T14:41:25.907+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Georgia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Atlanta"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/c87f40c2-6a24-46f3-b1bc-024df1ac1106","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/c87f40c2-6a24-46f3-b1bc-024df1ac1106/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Clinical Application Administrator </strong>at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>'s interoperability layer is what makes our network run. Every scan order that arrives from a referring physician, every radiology report delivered back to a provider, and every image routed through our PACS infrastructure depends on reliable integrations in production, every day. When they don't, patients wait longer, and providers lose trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As <strong>Clinical Application Administrator</strong>, you will be on the front line of keeping that infrastructure healthy. You will monitor HL7 interfaces, triage and resolve failures, manage the support queue, and work alongside engineering, operations, and clinical teams to close issues and prevent recurrence. You will also play a hands-on role in onboarding new imaging center clients, configuring and validating DICOM and HL7 gateway connections from deployment through live production.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a technically demanding operations role that rewards a deep curiosity about how clinical systems communicate with each other. You do not need to be a software engineer, but you need to be comfortable reading an HL7 message, diagnosing why it failed, and knowing what to do about it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and maintain active HL7 interfaces across ORM and ORU message types, ensuring orders and results are transmitted accurately and on time between <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> and partner systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze HL7 message segments, including PID, PV1, OBR, and OBX, to diagnose data transmission failures and validate downstream delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reprocess failed messages and confirm successful resolution, maintaining detailed records of the issue, root cause, and corrective action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform daily production support tasks, including report reprocessing, data corrections, and study transfers, to keep workflows running without interruption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the support ticket queue across Slack, Linear, and HubSpot, ensuring every issue has clear ownership, timely follow-up, and complete documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support PACS gateway operations alongside the Team Lead, including writing and maintaining scripts, pushing studies, troubleshooting connectivity issues, and validating image transfers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the technical deployment and configuration of DICOM and HL7 gateway software for new client onboarding, validating end-to-end image routing before go-live</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with engineering, operations, clinical, and client support teams to investigate and resolve integration issues, and to implement longer-term fixes where recurring patterns emerge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document processes, issue resolutions, and configuration changes to build a reliable knowledge base for the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities for automation and workflow improvement within the integration support function</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage smaller-scale projects end-to-end, providing coordination and communication across stakeholders from initiation through delivery</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Production fluency.</strong> Within 60 days, you independently triage and resolve the majority of incoming support tickets, demonstrating a clear understanding of our interface landscape, escalation paths, and documentation standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interface reliability.</strong> You have measurably reduced the average time to resolution for HL7 failures and reprocessing requests, and you have helped eliminate at least one category of recurring failures through improved monitoring or process changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Successful client onboardings.</strong> You have led the technical deployment and validation for new imaging center connections, completing them on schedule and with clean post-go-live performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Documentation depth.</strong> The team's knowledge base is materially better because of your time here. Process documentation, gateway configuration records, and issue resolution logs are complete, up to date, and actively used.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuous improvement contribution.</strong> You have identified and implemented at least one automation or workflow improvement that reduces manual effort in the support or onboarding process.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of HL7 v2 message structure, including common message types (ORM, ORU) and segment-level analysis (PID, PV1, OBR, OBX). You don't need to have built an interface engine from scratch, but you should be able to read a message and identify what's wrong with it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with an integration engine such as Rhapsody, Mirth Connect, or equivalent. Depth matters less than genuine familiarity and a clear appetite to develop further</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with PACS, RIS, or EHR systems and the radiology workflow they support: from order to acquisition to interpretation to results delivery. Understanding this lifecycle is essential context for diagnosing where things break</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with DICOM concepts and basic imaging terminology, including experience pushing, reprocessing, or validating imaging studies for troubleshooting purposes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational instincts. This role manages multiple concurrent issues across multiple platforms, and the person who thrives here keeps clear notes, closes loops, and doesn't let tickets go stale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear written and verbal communication. You will work across technical and non-technical stakeholders and need to translate between them accurately and without jargon where it isn't warranted</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in healthcare IT or clinical systems support is strongly preferred. Familiarity with the regulatory and operational context of healthcare makes a meaningful difference in this role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 2 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Amplified. AI is part of your daily workflow for drafting, analysis, and research, and you know how to check its output and use it responsibly with sensitive data. (most commercial, marketing, finance, people, and G&amp;A roles)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI is part of your daily default. You use it to draft, analyse, research, and pressure-test your own thinking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can show concrete examples where AI made your work meaningfully faster or better.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You know its failure modes: you check its work, and you don't paste sensitive data into public tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> We'll ask you to walk through how you'd use AI to tackle a real task from the role.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $75,000 - $90,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Clinical Application Administrator at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com's interoperability layer is what makes our network run. Every scan order that arrives from a referring physician, every radiology report delivered back to a provider, and every image routed through our PACS infrastructure depends on reliable integrations in production, every day. When they don't, patients wait longer, and providers lose trust.\n\n\n\nAs Clinical Application Administrator, you will be on the front line of keeping that infrastructure healthy. You will monitor HL7 interfaces, triage and resolve failures, manage the support queue, and work alongside engineering, operations, and clinical teams to close issues and prevent recurrence. You will also play a hands-on role in onboarding new imaging center clients, configuring and validating DICOM and HL7 gateway connections from deployment through live production.\n\n\n\nThis is a technically demanding operations role that rewards a deep curiosity about how clinical systems communicate with each other. You do not need to be a software engineer, but you need to be comfortable reading an HL7 message, diagnosing why it failed, and knowing what to do about it.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n\n\n - Monitor and maintain active HL7 interfaces across ORM and ORU message types, ensuring orders and results are transmitted accurately and on time between Scan.com http://Scan.com and partner systems\n\n - Analyze HL7 message segments, including PID, PV1, OBR, and OBX, to diagnose data transmission failures and validate downstream delivery\n\n - Reprocess failed messages and confirm successful resolution, maintaining detailed records of the issue, root cause, and corrective action\n\n - Perform daily production support tasks, including report reprocessing, data corrections, and study transfers, to keep workflows running without interruption\n\n - Manage the support ticket queue across Slack, Linear, and HubSpot, ensuring every issue has clear ownership, timely follow-up, and complete documentation\n\n - Support PACS gateway operations alongside the Team Lead, including writing and maintaining scripts, pushing studies, troubleshooting connectivity issues, and validating image transfers\n\n - Lead the technical deployment and configuration of DICOM and HL7 gateway software for new client onboarding, validating end-to-end image routing before go-live\n\n - Collaborate with engineering, operations, clinical, and client support teams to investigate and resolve integration issues, and to implement longer-term fixes where recurring patterns emerge\n\n - Document processes, issue resolutions, and configuration changes to build a reliable knowledge base for the team\n\n - Identify opportunities for automation and workflow improvement within the integration support function\n\n - Manage smaller-scale projects end-to-end, providing coordination and communication across stakeholders from initiation through delivery\n\n\n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR\n\n 1. Production fluency. Within 60 days, you independently triage and resolve the majority of incoming support tickets, demonstrating a clear understanding of our interface landscape, escalation paths, and documentation standards.\n\n 2. Interface reliability. You have measurably reduced the average time to resolution for HL7 failures and reprocessing requests, and you have helped eliminate at least one category of recurring failures through improved monitoring or process changes.\n\n 3. Successful client onboardings. You have led the technical deployment and validation for new imaging center connections, completing them on schedule and with clean post-go-live performance.\n\n 4. Documentation depth. The team's knowledge base is materially better because of your time here. Process documentation, gateway configuration records, and issue resolution logs are complete, up to date, and actively used.\n\n 5. Continuous improvement contribution. You have identified and implemented at least one automation or workflow improvement that reduces manual effort in the support or onboarding process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Working knowledge of HL7 v2 message structure, including common message types (ORM, ORU) and segment-level analysis (PID, PV1, OBR, OBX). You don't need to have built an interface engine from scratch, but you should be able to read a message and identify what's wrong with it\n\n - Experience with an integration engine such as Rhapsody, Mirth Connect, or equivalent. Depth matters less than genuine familiarity and a clear appetite to develop further\n\n - Familiarity with PACS, RIS, or EHR systems and the radiology workflow they support: from order to acquisition to interpretation to results delivery. Understanding this lifecycle is essential context for diagnosing where things break\n\n - Familiarity with DICOM concepts and basic imaging terminology, including experience pushing, reprocessing, or validating imaging studies for troubleshooting purposes\n\n - Strong organizational instincts. This role manages multiple concurrent issues across multiple platforms, and the person who thrives here keeps clear notes, closes loops, and doesn't let tickets go stale\n\n - Clear written and verbal communication. You will work across technical and non-technical stakeholders and need to translate between them accurately and without jargon where it isn't warranted\n\n - Experience in healthcare IT or clinical systems support is strongly preferred. Familiarity with the regulatory and operational context of healthcare makes a meaningful difference in this role\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 2 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Amplified. AI is part of your daily workflow for drafting, analysis, and research, and you know how to check its output and use it responsibly with sensitive data. (most commercial, marketing, finance, people, and G&A roles)\n   \n   - AI is part of your daily default. You use it to draft, analyse, research, and pressure-test your own thinking.\n   \n   - You can show concrete examples where AI made your work meaningfully faster or better.\n   \n   - You know its failure modes: you check its work, and you don't paste sensitive data into public tools.\n   \n   - Assessment: We'll ask you to walk through how you'd use AI to tackle a real task from the role.\n   \n   \n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at Scan.com http://Scan.com you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $75,000 - $90,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$80K – $90K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$80K - $90K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"654c94d2-7f85-40e3-859c-2bdef1452038","tierSummary":"$80K – $90K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"93509a7e-7321-4121-a883-54944d742a35","summary":"$80K – $90K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":90000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":90000}]}},{"id":"8f60ea2d-ce13-4f85-9112-f395651d80fb","title":"Product Operations Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-14T21:44:19.546+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/8f60ea2d-ce13-4f85-9112-f395651d80fb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/8f60ea2d-ce13-4f85-9112-f395651d80fb/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Product Operations Manager</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product Operations sits between strategy and execution. It is the function that turns a product team's intent into repeatable delivery and turns delivery into learning. At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, that work spans the full product surface, from acquisition and integrations to fulfillment and post-scan experiences, and it touches almost every function in the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As <strong>Product Operations Manager,</strong> you will partner closely with our product management team to build the rituals, documentation, and reporting infrastructure that make our product org run well. Your success will not be measured by how much you personally ship, but by how much better the teams around you ship because of the systems you put in place.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will suit someone who takes real pride in the craft of operations: someone who finds a well-written playbook satisfying, who can hold the details of five workstreams at once without losing context, and who already uses AI as a core part of their operational practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and coordinate rollout plans for new product features, working with PMs, Engineering, Design, and Operations to sequence launches, manage dependencies, and ensure the right teams are prepared to support what ships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain product documentation that supports both internal training and external communication, including feature briefs for internal enablement, release notes for partners and providers, and reference materials that keep stakeholders informed as the product evolves</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the data team to monitor post-release analytics, helping the product team understand whether launches are landing as intended and surfacing signals that suggest a feature needs iteration, promotion, or reconsideration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional sign-off for feature launches, ensuring the appropriate leaders across Engineering, Operations, Legal, and Clinical have reviewed and approved before release, with clear documentation of decisions and open items</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain a product knowledge base that is structured for AI agent consumption from day one, including designing information architecture that supports reliable retrieval, writing content that survives being chunked and re-assembled, and iterating on quality based on how well downstream agents perform against it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the product team on OKR planning and monitoring: helping to translate strategy into measurable objectives, tracking progress against them, flagging when priorities may need to shift, and reporting product impact to the wider organization in a way that builds shared understanding<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT TO SEE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A more predictable release rhythm.</strong> By the end of your first quarter, we would expect the product team to have a clearer, more repeatable cadence for rolling out features. Sign-offs happen at the right stage, the right people are informed, and launches feel less improvised.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A knowledge base that powers AI workflows.</strong> The documentation you produce is trusted by both humans and agents. Teams reference it before asking questions, and it already serves as the knowledge base for at least one AI-assisted workflow that meaningfully reduces manual effort within the product org.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A closer connection between launches and outcomes.</strong> In partnership with the data team, you will have helped establish a practice of reviewing post-release analytics for meaningful launches, so the product team consistently learns from what it ships rather than moving straight to the next thing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>OKR reporting that informs decisions.</strong> The wider organization has a clearer view of what the product team is working on, why, and how it is progressing. Reporting is timely and useful, and it supports genuine prioritization conversations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Trusted operator across the product org.</strong> Product managers rely on you to keep the machinery running, and cross-functional stakeholders trust the process you have built around launches and communication. Where things were previously ad hoc, they now feel intentional.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in product operations, program management, or a related operational role within a technology company, ideally one where you saw both the messy early stages and the transition toward more structured delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A genuine talent for written communication, including the patience to produce documentation that other people find clear, complete, and worth returning to. This role produces a lot of writing, and quality matters</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working with product and delivery metrics: you can partner with a data team to define what success looks like, interpret the results honestly, and communicate the story to stakeholders without either overstating or burying the findings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong coordination instincts across multiple stakeholders. You are the kind of person who notices when a sign-off is missing, when a launch dependency is drifting, or when a team needs a nudge, and you handle it without needing to be asked</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative disposition. Product operations depend on influence rather than authority, and you are comfortable working across PM, Engineering, Design, Operations, and Clinical stakeholders in a way that builds trust rather than friction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine AI fluency in your operational practice. You use AI tools daily, you have opinions about which ones work well for which tasks, and you have first-hand experience structuring information so that AI agents can consume it reliably. You can speak concretely about specific workflows you have improved with AI, and, ideally, about evaluation approaches you have used to assess output quality. Candidates who treat AI as an occasional aid rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in healthcare technology, medical imaging, or an adjacent regulated space is a plus, though strong operational fundamentals in another high-velocity domain are equally valued</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done because of it.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. To be successful at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2>WHAT WE OFFER</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $75,000 - $100,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Product Operations Manager at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nProduct Operations sits between strategy and execution. It is the function that turns a product team's intent into repeatable delivery and turns delivery into learning. At Scan.com http://Scan.com, that work spans the full product surface, from acquisition and integrations to fulfillment and post-scan experiences, and it touches almost every function in the company.\n\nAs Product Operations Manager, you will partner closely with our product management team to build the rituals, documentation, and reporting infrastructure that make our product org run well. Your success will not be measured by how much you personally ship, but by how much better the teams around you ship because of the systems you put in place.\n\nThis role will suit someone who takes real pride in the craft of operations: someone who finds a well-written playbook satisfying, who can hold the details of five workstreams at once without losing context, and who already uses AI as a core part of their operational practice.\n\n\n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Design and coordinate rollout plans for new product features, working with PMs, Engineering, Design, and Operations to sequence launches, manage dependencies, and ensure the right teams are prepared to support what ships\n\n - Create and maintain product documentation that supports both internal training and external communication, including feature briefs for internal enablement, release notes for partners and providers, and reference materials that keep stakeholders informed as the product evolves\n\n - Partner with the data team to monitor post-release analytics, helping the product team understand whether launches are landing as intended and surfacing signals that suggest a feature needs iteration, promotion, or reconsideration\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional sign-off for feature launches, ensuring the appropriate leaders across Engineering, Operations, Legal, and Clinical have reviewed and approved before release, with clear documentation of decisions and open items\n\n - Build and maintain a product knowledge base that is structured for AI agent consumption from day one, including designing information architecture that supports reliable retrieval, writing content that survives being chunked and re-assembled, and iterating on quality based on how well downstream agents perform against it\n\n - Support the product team on OKR planning and monitoring: helping to translate strategy into measurable objectives, tracking progress against them, flagging when priorities may need to shift, and reporting product impact to the wider organization in a way that builds shared understanding\n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT TO SEE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR\n\n 1. A more predictable release rhythm. By the end of your first quarter, we would expect the product team to have a clearer, more repeatable cadence for rolling out features. Sign-offs happen at the right stage, the right people are informed, and launches feel less improvised.\n\n 2. A knowledge base that powers AI workflows. The documentation you produce is trusted by both humans and agents. Teams reference it before asking questions, and it already serves as the knowledge base for at least one AI-assisted workflow that meaningfully reduces manual effort within the product org.\n\n 3. A closer connection between launches and outcomes. In partnership with the data team, you will have helped establish a practice of reviewing post-release analytics for meaningful launches, so the product team consistently learns from what it ships rather than moving straight to the next thing.\n\n 4. OKR reporting that informs decisions. The wider organization has a clearer view of what the product team is working on, why, and how it is progressing. Reporting is timely and useful, and it supports genuine prioritization conversations.\n\n 5. Trusted operator across the product org. Product managers rely on you to keep the machinery running, and cross-functional stakeholders trust the process you have built around launches and communication. Where things were previously ad hoc, they now feel intentional.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Experience in product operations, program management, or a related operational role within a technology company, ideally one where you saw both the messy early stages and the transition toward more structured delivery\n\n - A genuine talent for written communication, including the patience to produce documentation that other people find clear, complete, and worth returning to. This role produces a lot of writing, and quality matters\n\n - Comfort working with product and delivery metrics: you can partner with a data team to define what success looks like, interpret the results honestly, and communicate the story to stakeholders without either overstating or burying the findings\n\n - Strong coordination instincts across multiple stakeholders. You are the kind of person who notices when a sign-off is missing, when a launch dependency is drifting, or when a team needs a nudge, and you handle it without needing to be asked\n\n - A collaborative disposition. Product operations depend on influence rather than authority, and you are comfortable working across PM, Engineering, Design, Operations, and Clinical stakeholders in a way that builds trust rather than friction\n\n - Genuine AI fluency in your operational practice. You use AI tools daily, you have opinions about which ones work well for which tasks, and you have first-hand experience structuring information so that AI agents can consume it reliably. You can speak concretely about specific workflows you have improved with AI, and, ideally, about evaluation approaches you have used to assess output quality. Candidates who treat AI as an occasional aid rather than a core part of how they work will not be competitive for this role.\n\n - Prior experience in healthcare technology, medical imaging, or an adjacent regulated space is a plus, though strong operational fundamentals in another high-velocity domain are equally valued\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done because of it.\n\n - Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)\n   \n   - You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.\n   \n   - You can explain a workflow you redesigned so that a machine does the boring 80%.\n   \n   - You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.\n   \n   - Assessment: a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. To be successful at Scan.com http://Scan.com, you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $75,000 - $100,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$90K – $120K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$90K - $120K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f7374a58-6211-4396-9489-5839cfe535fd","tierSummary":"$90K – $120K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"92d6bf00-326a-4eaf-8cff-a9ce7776c653","summary":"$90K – $120K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":120000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":120000}]}},{"id":"4fed9a63-4146-4cbc-9089-d629e55100d2","title":"Data Engineer II","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-29T21:08:11.810+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/4fed9a63-4146-4cbc-9089-d629e55100d2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/4fed9a63-4146-4cbc-9089-d629e55100d2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a <strong>Data Engineer </strong>at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is a full-stack discipline. We don't have analysts who hand off to engineers to build the model, or engineers who hand off to analysts to build the dashboard. As a <strong>Data Engineer</strong>, you will own the work end-to-end, from raw source data through the transformation layer, through the product that a stakeholder uses to make a decision.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our data team supports every function across the US and UK: operations, revenue cycle, marketing, sales, provider success, and product. We sit at the center of a fast-moving business, and the work ranges from answering a precise operational question to building the automated reporting infrastructure that makes that question answerable without us in the loop next time.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We use a modern tech stack: Fivetran and Python for ingestion, Snowflake as our data warehouse, dbt for transformations, GitHub for CI/CD, Tableau for visualizations, and Cursor, Claude, and Snowflake Cortex for AI-assisted development. Our source systems span Postgres, HubSpot, Front, Acuity, Dialpad, and Facebook and Google Ads.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dbt models that transform raw source data into reliable, well-documented, tested analytical assets used across the business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with stakeholders across Operations, Finance, Marketing, Sales, and Product to translate ambiguous business questions into precise analytical deliverables. You should be able to identify if the ask needs refinement before the work begins</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and ship Tableau dashboards and data products that automate reporting that currently requires manual effort, permanently removing recurring analytical burden from the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify gaps in our data coverage and work with engineering or independently to close them. This can mean writing a Python ingestion pipeline or modeling a new source</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain data quality standards across the warehouse: write dbt tests, monitor for anomalies, and ensure that the numbers stakeholders see are trustworthy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the team's analytical infrastructure. This means shared macros, source definitions, documentation standards, and CI/CD practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stretch into various data science or data engineering projects based on business demand and based on your own personal development: pipeline development, ML feature preparation, or predictive modeling.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep business context. Within 90 days, you understand the unit economics, operational workflows, and key performance drivers across the functions you support. You can receive a stakeholder request and immediately identify whether it's answerable with existing models, requires new modeling work, or requires a better-defined question.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable analytical infrastructure. You have meaningfully improved the coverage, test depth, and documentation of our dbt model layer — making it easier for the next analyst to build on your work and reducing the frequency of data quality incidents.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High-impact data products shipped. Several Tableau dashboards or analytical products are in production and actively used by stakeholders to make decisions, replacing manual reporting or filling a genuine analytical gap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Automation wins. You have identified and eliminated at least one recurring manual reporting process, replacing it with a scheduled, automated output that runs without human intervention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Trusted analytical partner. Stakeholders across the business seek out your input before they finalize requirements, not after. You are known for asking the right clarifying questions and delivering work that answers the real question, not just the stated one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong SQL: you write complex queries fluently, understand query performance, and don't need a template to construct a multi-stage transformation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with a modern data transformation tool, ideally dbt or SQLMesh. You understand the model DAG, have written tests and documentation, and are familiar with CI/CD practices in a transformation layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a modern cloud data warehouse, ideally Snowflake or BigQuery — you understand how storage and compute interact and can write warehouse-idiomatic SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with a BI tool such as Tableau, Metabase, Sigma, or Omni — you can design a dashboard that stakeholders actually use, not just one that technically answers the question</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong stakeholder instincts: you have worked directly with non-technical stakeholders to scope and deliver analytical work, and you know how to translate between business language and data model logic</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Python for data work. Ingestion pipelines with libraries like dlt, pandas-based transformation scripts, or scripted automation of manual reporting processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup experience is a plus. You are comfortable with ambiguity, can prioritize without perfect information, and don't need a fully defined ticket to get started</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare experience is a plus, particularly in imaging, RCM, or provider operations — but strong analytical fundamentals in any high-velocity domain are equally valued</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>AI REQUIREMENTS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can explain a workflow you redesigned so a machine does the boring 80%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $140,000 - $160,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for a Data Engineer at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nData at Scan.com http://Scan.com is a full-stack discipline. We don't have analysts who hand off to engineers to build the model, or engineers who hand off to analysts to build the dashboard. As a Data Engineer, you will own the work end-to-end, from raw source data through the transformation layer, through the product that a stakeholder uses to make a decision.\n\n \n\nOur data team supports every function across the US and UK: operations, revenue cycle, marketing, sales, provider success, and product. We sit at the center of a fast-moving business, and the work ranges from answering a precise operational question to building the automated reporting infrastructure that makes that question answerable without us in the loop next time.\n\n \n\nWe use a modern tech stack: Fivetran and Python for ingestion, Snowflake as our data warehouse, dbt for transformations, GitHub for CI/CD, Tableau for visualizations, and Cursor, Claude, and Snowflake Cortex for AI-assisted development. Our source systems span Postgres, HubSpot, Front, Acuity, Dialpad, and Facebook and Google Ads.\n\n \n\nAs a scale-up business, you can expect your role to develop over time. Here are some of the types of things you could be getting involved in:\n\n - Build and maintain dbt models that transform raw source data into reliable, well-documented, tested analytical assets used across the business\n\n - Partner with stakeholders across Operations, Finance, Marketing, Sales, and Product to translate ambiguous business questions into precise analytical deliverables. You should be able to identify if the ask needs refinement before the work begins\n\n - Design and ship Tableau dashboards and data products that automate reporting that currently requires manual effort, permanently removing recurring analytical burden from the team\n\n - Identify gaps in our data coverage and work with engineering or independently to close them. This can mean writing a Python ingestion pipeline or modeling a new source\n\n - Maintain data quality standards across the warehouse: write dbt tests, monitor for anomalies, and ensure that the numbers stakeholders see are trustworthy\n\n - Contribute to the team's analytical infrastructure. This means shared macros, source definitions, documentation standards, and CI/CD practices.\n\n - Stretch into various data science or data engineering projects based on business demand and based on your own personal development: pipeline development, ML feature preparation, or predictive modeling.\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE\n\n 1. Deep business context. Within 90 days, you understand the unit economics, operational workflows, and key performance drivers across the functions you support. You can receive a stakeholder request and immediately identify whether it's answerable with existing models, requires new modeling work, or requires a better-defined question.\n\n 2. Reliable analytical infrastructure. You have meaningfully improved the coverage, test depth, and documentation of our dbt model layer — making it easier for the next analyst to build on your work and reducing the frequency of data quality incidents.\n\n 3. High-impact data products shipped. Several Tableau dashboards or analytical products are in production and actively used by stakeholders to make decisions, replacing manual reporting or filling a genuine analytical gap.\n\n 4. Automation wins. You have identified and eliminated at least one recurring manual reporting process, replacing it with a scheduled, automated output that runs without human intervention.\n\n 5. Trusted analytical partner. Stakeholders across the business seek out your input before they finalize requirements, not after. You are known for asking the right clarifying questions and delivering work that answers the real question, not just the stated one.\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - Strong SQL: you write complex queries fluently, understand query performance, and don't need a template to construct a multi-stage transformation\n\n - Hands-on experience with a modern data transformation tool, ideally dbt or SQLMesh. You understand the model DAG, have written tests and documentation, and are familiar with CI/CD practices in a transformation layer\n\n - Experience with a modern cloud data warehouse, ideally Snowflake or BigQuery — you understand how storage and compute interact and can write warehouse-idiomatic SQL\n\n - Proficiency with a BI tool such as Tableau, Metabase, Sigma, or Omni — you can design a dashboard that stakeholders actually use, not just one that technically answers the question\n\n - Strong stakeholder instincts: you have worked directly with non-technical stakeholders to scope and deliver analytical work, and you know how to translate between business language and data model logic\n\n - Python for data work. Ingestion pipelines with libraries like dlt, pandas-based transformation scripts, or scripted automation of manual reporting processes\n\n - For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop.\n\n - Startup experience is a plus. You are comfortable with ambiguity, can prioritize without perfect information, and don't need a fully defined ticket to get started\n\n - Healthcare experience is a plus, particularly in imaging, RCM, or provider operations — but strong analytical fundamentals in any high-velocity domain are equally valued\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 1 — For this role, the expectation is that you are an AI-Native. You build with AI directly, shipping, automating, or prototyping real work with LLMs and agents, and have clear judgment on where humans must stay in the loop. (this is typically aligned to engineering, data, product, ops automation, RevOps)\n   \n   - You build with AI, not just alongside it. You've shipped, automated, or prototyped something real using LLMs, agents, or AI tooling.\n   \n   - You can explain a workflow you redesigned so a machine does the boring 80%.\n   \n   - You have a view on where agentic systems help and where a human must stay in the loop, especially in regulated, PHI-adjacent work.\n   \n   - Assessment: a practical exercise where you use AI tools live or in a take-home.\n\n\n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at Scan.com http://Scan.com you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do your best work, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call is via telephone and will last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, length varies depending on how many people and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $140,000 - $160,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$130K – $150K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$130K - $150K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"883c0e52-8d4f-437a-b232-42331d7201f8","tierSummary":"$130K – $150K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"3b05a2ee-343d-444c-adf3-9a271669e501","summary":"$130K – $150K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":150000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":150000}]}},{"id":"e3460b05-078d-4050-ab6a-e62a0f8733a7","title":"Associate Product Manager","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-25T17:22:25.101+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"10001","addressRegion":"New York","streetAddress":"368 9th Ave","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/e3460b05-078d-4050-ab6a-e62a0f8733a7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/scan-com/e3460b05-078d-4050-ab6a-e62a0f8733a7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an<strong> Associate Product Manager</strong> at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Millions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The <strong>Associate Product Manager</strong> program at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is designed for people who are early in their product careers but not early in their product thinking. If you are one to four years into your professional career, whether that time was spent in a product role or in an adjacent discipline you are now pivoting from, and you have spent serious time developing the craft, this program is built for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an APM at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, you will be embedded on a product team from day one, working across the surface of our business: marketplace, integrations, provider tools, patient experience, and the AI-driven internal systems that increasingly power all of it. Some of the things you will get involved in:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a defined slice of a product team's roadmap under the guidance of a senior PM, taking work from problem discovery through shipped outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write PRDs, run discovery and user research, and partner with engineering, design, and operations to translate ambiguous problems into concrete product decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to prioritization and roadmap conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrument what you ship, track outcomes rigorously, and close the loop between what launched and what changed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI as a first-class instrument across the full PM workflow, including discovery synthesis, data analysis, PRD drafting, prototype exploration, competitive analysis, and quality evaluation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop deep substance in healthtech and medical imaging, building the informed product judgment that separates competent PMs from great ones in this domain</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow into full PM ownership over the course of the program, with a clear line of sight to the next role</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>WHAT WE ARE INVESTING IN YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our APM program prioritizes accelerating your career growth. We do this by giving you:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthtech and imaging context. You will get structured onboarding to the substance of the domain: how radiology works, how imaging centers operate, how the referral economy functions, and case studies of successful B2B and B2C healthtech companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product coaching. You will receive consistent coaching from senior product leaders, focused on the specific gaps in your craft. Expect regular pairing sessions with senior PMs, with independent time in between sessions to master various skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An accelerated growth plan. The program is designed to compress the path from Associate to senior product ownership. We will invest deliberately in the areas that most hinder your progression, and we will be direct with you about what is working and what is not.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE</strong></h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shipped product outcomes that matter.</strong> By the end of your first year, you will have shipped work that meaningfully moved a metric or unlocked a capability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Genuine product judgment in imaging.</strong> You have moved from learning the domain to having real points of view about it. Senior team members are asking for your take on domain questions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI mastery that raises the team's bar.</strong> You are using AI across your workflow at a level that other PMs learn from. The way you work influences how the broader product function operates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Trust across engineering and design.</strong> Your engineering and design partners view you as a credible collaborator whose PRDs, prioritization decisions, and feedback improve their work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Visible growth.</strong> Your capability at the end of year one is meaningfully greater than at the start, and you can articulate that growth concretely, with specific examples of decisions, artifacts, and instincts that have sharpened.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>WHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth role, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">One to four years of total professional experience. That time could have been spent in an APM or Associate role at another company, in an adjacent role with real product surface area (founder, early operator, technical or design contributor with product ownership), or in a different discipline you are now pivoting from. What matters here is total career stage, not just product career stage: this program is built for early-career professionals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep familiarity with the discipline of product management. You have gone well beyond the introductory content and can speak concretely about frameworks and specific approaches you use. You are ready to be assessed as someone with 1,000+ hours of intentional development in the craft.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-native skills as a baseline. You are past the \"AI as prompt assistant\" stage. Your PM workflow, including discovery, research synthesis, data analysis, drafting, prototyping, competitive scans, and evaluation of AI outputs themselves, has been rebuilt around AI as a core instrument. You can demonstrate this concretely, and you will be asked to. Applicants still learning to prompt effectively will not be competitive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical instincts. You've directly queried raw data to solve business problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written communication. You can turn a fuzzy problem into a clear PRD, and you value outstanding exposition.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A trajectory-first mindset. You see this program as one step on a longer path toward product leadership or founding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience or a genuine interest in healthcare technology, medical imaging, marketplaces, or interoperability is a plus, though not required</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>AI REQUIREMENTS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tier 2 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Amplified. AI is part of your daily workflow for drafting, analysis, and research, and you know how to check its output and use it responsibly with sensitive data. (most commercial, marketing, finance, people, and G&amp;A roles)</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI is part of your daily default. You use it to draft, analyse, research, and pressure-test your own thinking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can show concrete examples where AI made your work meaningfully faster or better.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You know its failure modes: you check its work, and you don't paste sensitive data into public tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Assessment:</strong> We'll ask you to walk through how you'd use AI to tackle a real task from the role.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>A VIEW ON OUR CULTURE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://scan.com\"> </a><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><u>Scan.com</u></a><u>,</u> you must embody our values.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>OUR VALUES</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Always Play Offense</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build with the Best</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You trust your colleagues to deliver.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care Deeply, Challenge Directly</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Embrace Growth, Be Curious</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Push the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:</p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call will be by telephone and last around 30 minutes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a>. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, the length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>WHAT WE OFFER</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary range of $110,000 - $120,000</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible remote or hybrid work options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dedicated personal development budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, vision, and dental coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401k retirement plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All the equipment you need to do your best work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>DIVERSITY AT </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\"><strong>SCAN.COM</strong></a></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Scan.com\">Scan.com</a> is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"mailto:people@scan.com\">people@scan.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look forward to receiving your application!</p>","descriptionPlain":"We're Scan.com http://Scan.com.  We're building America's national imaging network: the infrastructure that connects patients, providers, and payers to faster, better-value diagnostic imaging.  Thousands of patients move through our platform every day, and each is a real person waiting for an answer to a healthcare concern. We exist to get them that answer faster.\n\n\n\nWe manage the medical imaging pathway end-to-end.  Providers order through a single point of entry, and from there, we run the entire medical diagnostic pathway.  Managing the full pathway, rather than brokering pieces of it, is what lets us deliver imaging faster, at higher quality, and at a lower cost than the fragmented status quo.\n\n\n\nWe're looking for an Associate Product Manager at an exciting time. We've raised over $200m in funding to date, reached profitability, and are growing 100% year on year.\n\nMillions of people wait too long for a diagnosis. Come help us fix that.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL BE GETTING INVOLVED IN\n\nThe Associate Product Manager program at Scan.com http://Scan.com is designed for people who are early in their product careers but not early in their product thinking. If you are one to four years into your professional career, whether that time was spent in a product role or in an adjacent discipline you are now pivoting from, and you have spent serious time developing the craft, this program is built for you.\n\nAs an APM at Scan.com http://Scan.com, you will be embedded on a product team from day one, working across the surface of our business: marketplace, integrations, provider tools, patient experience, and the AI-driven internal systems that increasingly power all of it. Some of the things you will get involved in:\n\n - Own a defined slice of a product team's roadmap under the guidance of a senior PM, taking work from problem discovery through shipped outcomes\n\n - Write PRDs, run discovery and user research, and partner with engineering, design, and operations to translate ambiguous problems into concrete product decisions\n\n - Contribute to prioritization and roadmap conversations\n\n - Instrument what you ship, track outcomes rigorously, and close the loop between what launched and what changed\n\n - Use AI as a first-class instrument across the full PM workflow, including discovery synthesis, data analysis, PRD drafting, prototype exploration, competitive analysis, and quality evaluation.\n\n - Develop deep substance in healthtech and medical imaging, building the informed product judgment that separates competent PMs from great ones in this domain\n\n - Grow into full PM ownership over the course of the program, with a clear line of sight to the next role\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE ARE INVESTING IN YOU\n\nOur APM program prioritizes accelerating your career growth. We do this by giving you:\n\n - Healthtech and imaging context. You will get structured onboarding to the substance of the domain: how radiology works, how imaging centers operate, how the referral economy functions, and case studies of successful B2B and B2C healthtech companies.\n\n - Product coaching. You will receive consistent coaching from senior product leaders, focused on the specific gaps in your craft. Expect regular pairing sessions with senior PMs, with independent time in between sessions to master various skills.\n\n - An accelerated growth plan. The program is designed to compress the path from Associate to senior product ownership. We will invest deliberately in the areas that most hinder your progression, and we will be direct with you about what is working and what is not.\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE TOP 5 THINGS WE WANT YOU TO ACHIEVE IN YOUR FIRST YEAR ARE\n\n 1. Shipped product outcomes that matter. By the end of your first year, you will have shipped work that meaningfully moved a metric or unlocked a capability.\n\n 2. Genuine product judgment in imaging. You have moved from learning the domain to having real points of view about it. Senior team members are asking for your take on domain questions.\n\n 3. AI mastery that raises the team's bar. You are using AI across your workflow at a level that other PMs learn from. The way you work influences how the broader product function operates.\n\n 4. Trust across engineering and design. Your engineering and design partners view you as a credible collaborator whose PRDs, prioritization decisions, and feedback improve their work.\n\n 5. Visible growth. Your capability at the end of year one is meaningfully greater than at the start, and you can articulate that growth concretely, with specific examples of decisions, artifacts, and instincts that have sharpened.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU MIGHT BRING TO THE TABLE\n\nYou don't need to tick all the boxes to apply for this role. Whether it's your first role or your fifth role, we believe everyone can add value, learn, and grow. However, these might be some of the ways you are currently adding value:\n\n - One to four years of total professional experience. That time could have been spent in an APM or Associate role at another company, in an adjacent role with real product surface area (founder, early operator, technical or design contributor with product ownership), or in a different discipline you are now pivoting from. What matters here is total career stage, not just product career stage: this program is built for early-career professionals\n\n - Deep familiarity with the discipline of product management. You have gone well beyond the introductory content and can speak concretely about frameworks and specific approaches you use. You are ready to be assessed as someone with 1,000+ hours of intentional development in the craft.\n\n - AI-native skills as a baseline. You are past the \"AI as prompt assistant\" stage. Your PM workflow, including discovery, research synthesis, data analysis, drafting, prototyping, competitive scans, and evaluation of AI outputs themselves, has been rebuilt around AI as a core instrument. You can demonstrate this concretely, and you will be asked to. Applicants still learning to prompt effectively will not be competitive.\n\n - Strong analytical instincts. You've directly queried raw data to solve business problems.\n\n - Excellent written communication. You can turn a fuzzy problem into a clear PRD, and you value outstanding exposition.\n\n - A trajectory-first mindset. You see this program as one step on a longer path toward product leadership or founding.\n\n - Prior experience or a genuine interest in healthcare technology, medical imaging, marketplaces, or interoperability is a plus, though not required\n\n\n\n\nAI REQUIREMENTS\n\nAt Scan.com http://Scan.com, AI isn't a side project; it's how we work. We expect everyone to use AI to think faster, remove drudgery, and multiply their output. What we care about is judgment: knowing when AI makes you sharper, when it doesn't, and how to use it responsibly around patient data. We'll assess this in the way that matters for this role, using the tier below. You don't need to be an engineer. You need to be someone who reaches for the best tool and gets more done as a result.\n\n - Tier 2 — For this role, the expectation is that you are AI-Amplified. AI is part of your daily workflow for drafting, analysis, and research, and you know how to check its output and use it responsibly with sensitive data. (most commercial, marketing, finance, people, and G&A roles)\n   \n   - AI is part of your daily default. You use it to draft, analyse, research, and pressure-test your own thinking.\n   \n   - You can show concrete examples where AI made your work meaningfully faster or better.\n   \n   - You know its failure modes: you check its work, and you don't paste sensitive data into public tools.\n   \n   - Assessment: We'll ask you to walk through how you'd use AI to tackle a real task from the role.\n\n\n\n\nA VIEW ON OUR CULTURE\n\nWe're building something that matters. Every scan we speed up is a real person waiting on an answer, and that urgency runs through everything we do. We move fast, we own outcomes, and take pride in our output. If you like ambiguity, working with ambitious people, and want your work to visibly move the needle, you'll feel at home here. For you to be successful at  http://scan.comScan.com http://Scan.com, you must embody our values.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\nAlways Play Offense\n\nIf we're not growing, we're dying. Everyone needs a bias for action. Speed and momentum, combined with quality execution, propel our business forward.\n\n - You don't quit on hard problems. Fail fast, dust off, go again.\n\n - You celebrate wins, then seek the next opportunity.\n\n - You see it, you fix it. No task is beneath you, at any level.\n\nBuild with the Best\n\nThe company we build is the team we build. If we don't have the right people in the right seats, doing the right things, we will fail.\n\n - Talent recognizes talent. You actively bring quality hires into the business.\n\n - You trust your colleagues to deliver.\n\n - You open-source your knowledge. You're never a single point of failure.\n\nCare Deeply, Challenge Directly\n\nCare enough to have the hard conversations, and don't dwell on them. Don't go up the chain to communicate. Go straight to the person.\n\n - Strong opinions, weakly held. You welcome challenge and feedback.\n\n - You get to the point: direct challenge plus an alternative solution.\n\n - You ask \"why\". Before calling something bad, understand why it exists.\n\nEmbrace Growth, Be Curious\n\nPush the limits of your understanding and potential, and you will be supported to get better.\n\n - You proactively seek feedback, whatever your level.\n\n - You invest in understanding our business: teams, customers, processes.\n\n - You invest in your own growth and are willing to unlearn.\n\nWe're a high-performing team with low ego. We hire people who are brilliant and kind, who give it straight, back it up with evidence, and change their mind when the facts change. We'll give you real ownership early, the tools to do the best work of your career, and colleagues who raise your game. In return, we ask for high standards, genuine care for patients and each other, and the drive to leave things better than you found them. If that sounds like you, let’s talk!\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE WILL INTERVIEW YOU\n\nWe keep our interview process short and sweet, and we're a nimble team that can progress at pace. Here are the stages you can expect, but we might switch up the order of each step depending on team availability:\n\n 1. Introductory call/interview with our Senior Talent Partner. The call will be by telephone and last around 30 minutes.\n\n 2. Should it feel like there is an initial fit for all, we will invite you to a video call with the hiring manager for around 45 minutes. This is a more structured interview that will deep-dive into the role and technical needs.\n\n 3. 'Scan Standard' interview, where our panel screens for values alignment and the success factors that matter at Scan.com http://Scan.com. You will also be assessed on your AI fluency at the stage and depth relevant to your role (see AI Requirements above).\n\n 4. Meet the founders and/or other team members. Again, the length varies depending on how many people are involved and whether in person or via video call.\n\n 5. Offer!\n    \n    \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\nWe go beyond the basics with our benefits package. We believe great work starts with supporting our people. Here's what you can expect from us:\n\n - Salary range of $110,000 - $120,000\n\n - Flexible remote or hybrid work options\n\n - Dedicated personal development budget\n\n - Medical, vision, and dental coverage\n\n - 28+ days of paid time off across PTO and wellbeing days, so you can show up at your best\n\n - Paid parental leave\n\n - 401k retirement plan\n\n - All the equipment you need to do your best work\n\n - Inclusive, people-first policies designed by our team, for our team\n\n\n\n\nDIVERSITY AT SCAN.COM http://Scan.com\n\nScan.com http://Scan.com is committed to eliminating discrimination and encouraging diversity within our team. We strive to provide equality and fairness for all job applicants and employees and never discriminate on the basis of gender, marital status, age, race, ethnicity, religion, or physical differences.\n\nWe are opposed to all forms of unlawful treatment and discrimination.\n\nOur ambition is for our team to be representative of society's diversity, and for every employee to feel respected and able to bring their best selves to work.\n\nIf you need an accommodation to apply or interview, contact us at people@scan.com.\n\nWe look forward to receiving your application!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$110K – $120K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$110K - $120K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"67a3fc6c-3d18-4100-b4b6-af7aff40a882","tierSummary":"$110K – $120K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"09866199-9a43-4c83-bfb1-2c8db99cc472","summary":"$110K – $120K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":120000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":110000,"maxValue":120000}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}